Attribution: imessage-exporter
------------------------------

Parts of Chattr's iMessage support are derived from imessage-exporter,
Copyright (C) Christopher Sardegna, licensed under the GNU General Public
License, version 3 or later:

    https://github.com/ReagentX/imessage-exporter

Derived portions (from the imessage-exporter 2.x series):

  - src/imessage_tools.py: the DatabaseDiagnostics class (diagnostic
    sections, their order and their output wording), including its
    attachment path resolution and file size formatting.
  - src/parsers/imessage_database_parser.py: the structure of the message
    query (column selection and aliases, and the newest-schema-first
    fallback), the parsing of tapback target identifiers ("p:N/GUID"), and
    one code comment about handle ID 0.

Derived portions (from imessage-exporter 5.0.1):

  - src/chattr/imessage_schema.py: probing the live schema and composing the
    message query from the columns that exist (tables/capabilities.rs,
    tables/messages/columns.rs).
  - src/chattr/imessage_groups.py: grouping handle rows that are one person
    and merging chats that are one conversation (tables/handle.rs,
    tables/chat_handle.rs, docs/tables/duplicates.md).
  - src/chattr/imessage_events.py: reading edit history from
    message_summary_info and turning event rows into sentences
    (message_types/edited.rs, tables/messages/models/group_action.rs,
    tables/messages/message.rs).
  - src/chattr/imessage_payload.py: unarchiving NSKeyedArchiver payloads and
    reading link previews and app messages; the table of balloon bundle ids
    and send effects (util/plist.rs, message_types/url.rs,
    message_types/app.rs, tables/messages/message.rs).
  - src/chattr/people.py, Contacts.from_macos: reading the macOS Contacts
    databases (the exporter's app/contacts.rs).

Elsewhere, knowledge of Apple's iMessage database layout (tables, columns,
timestamp encoding, tapback codes) was learned in part by studying
imessage-exporter. Chattr's other features, such as spam filtering, vCard
contact resolution, group detection, attachment conversion and reports,
and HTML output, are its own.


